.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_RESUME 3 "2026-07-18" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_resume \- resume event delivery for a registration previously paused by ccol_event_loop_pause
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_event_loop_resume(ccol_event_loop loop, ccol_event_reg reg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Works only on fd registrations. A registration made from a queue or a
ccol_channel selectable gives ccol_invalid_args, the same restriction
that ccol_event_loop_modify has.

Recomputes the fd's combined epoll interest mask with reg included
again. That is an ordinary EPOLL_CTL_MOD call when the fd is in
the kernel's epoll interest set, which happens when the other direction
on the fd is live and not paused, and an EPOLL_CTL_ADD call when
ccol_event_loop_pause took the fd out of the set because every
direction was paused. reg's direction, its generation and its share of
ccol_event_loop_reg_count stay as they were before the pause; the call
only undoes what ccol_event_loop_pause did to the interest mask.

It also re-arms a reg that the loop stopped watching because an event
reached it that none of its handlers can take (see
ccol_event_loop_add(3)).

Resuming a reg that is neither paused nor stopped that way (one that
was never paused, or was already resumed) succeeds and does nothing, on
purpose. It matches how ccol_event_loop_modify treats a request for the
state that a registration is already in.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop the registration belongs to.
reg   Registration to resume.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        reg is resumed, or it was not paused.
ccol_invalid_args   loop is CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_NULL, a stale handle,
                    or a handle that has already been destroyed;
                    or reg is CCOL_EVENT_REG_NULL or fails to
                    resolve for another reason; or reg is a
                    registration for a queue or a ccol_channel. A reg
                    that fails to resolve includes one removed at the
                    same time, for example when the connection is
                    closed while the caller thinks it still owns a
                    paused registration to resume.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call at the same time as ccol_event_loop_remove(), and from a
callback running on one of the reactor threads. It is common to call it
from a different thread than the one that paused reg, as in the
EXAMPLES section of ccol_event_loop_pause(3).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_pause (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_modify (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_reg_generation (3)
